1010:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/ipv4/ip4.c **** /**
1011:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/ipv4/ip4.c ****  * Simple interface to ip_output_if. It finds the outgoing network
1012:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/ipv4/ip4.c ****  * interface and calls upon ip_output_if to do the actual work.
1013:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/ipv4/ip4.c ****  *
1014:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/ipv4/ip4.c ****  * @param p the packet to send (p->payload points to the data, e.g. next
1015:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/ipv4/ip4.c ****             protocol header; if dest == LWIP_IP_HDRINCL, p already includes an
1016:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/ipv4/ip4.c ****             IP header and p->payload points to that IP header)
1017:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/ipv4/ip4.c ****  * @param src the source IP address to send from (if src == IP4_ADDR_ANY, the
1018:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/ipv4/ip4.c ****  *         IP  address of the netif used to send is used as source address)
1019:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/ipv4/ip4.c ****  * @param dest the destination IP address to send the packet to
1020:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/ipv4/ip4.c ****  * @param ttl the TTL value to be set in the IP header
1021:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/ipv4/ip4.c ****  * @param tos the TOS value to be set in the IP header
1022:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/ipv4/ip4.c ****  * @param proto the PROTOCOL to be set in the IP header
1023:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/ipv4/ip4.c ****  *
1024:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/ipv4/ip4.c ****  * @return ERR_RTE if no route is found
1025:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/ipv4/ip4.c ****  *         see ip_output_if() for more return values
1026:./lwip-2.1.2/src/core/ipv4/ip4.c ****  */
